ontv\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.facebook.com/groups/sciontv </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> This is the official Facebook group for Scion: The TV Series (http://scion-tv.com/), brought to you by Jenkins &amp; Tate (https://www.jenkinsandtate.com) and Onyx Path Publishing... </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If it wasn't one of these, it wasn't operated by us.<br /> <br /> I don't recall booting anyone recently and I don't think the other admins have either, so I suspect it was a fan group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-21T14:34:15-07:00","id":1449210,"title":"","content":"No IanWatson I don\u2019t think it was one of those. The Admin had a post up telling everyone they had to answer the question and if they had any pictures of the confederate flag on there home page they would not be allowed in. I posted that this was wrong that you shouldn\u2019t judge by such things be instead judge by their actions in the group. I was than called a racist and a Homophobe because I stuck up for freedom of beliefs. Someone else posted a stupid article claiming to tolerance is wrong and we should attack people that believe things we consider wrong. My comments were all along the lines that it\u2019s actions not beliefs that matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6379-tytalan","name":"tytalan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T08:54:54-07:00","id":1449257,"title":"","content":"To be fair, white supremacy (which is what a Confederate flag represents) is not a belief system I want to interact with, in RPG fandom or anywhere else. At some point, we have to make a choice about who is allowed to feel welcome at our gaming tables. If we let white nationalists feel welcome &quot;so long as they don't cause trouble,&quot; than the people their ideology targets won't feel welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24383-laughinggull","name":"LaughingGull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24383_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T09:57:39-07:00","id":1449265,"title":"","content":"Well, while I agree with you in many levels, excluding people because of their background is not cool, no matter what.<br /> <br /> If you want to establish a connection and prove all kind of people are equal and deserve respect, you must talk about it to the people that don\u2019t agree. It\u2019s easy to deal with people equal minded, but basically nobody learns anything from this, as there is nothing new to be learned (at least in that aspect of the conversation). The only way to prove to a racist that others are worth is by showing they are worth, forcing it down only creates more \u201cpath to the dark side\u201d (fear -&gt; hate -&gt; prejudice).<br /> <br /> The correct path is a very hard one, involving years of continuous effort, not exclusion, not talking down, not forcing things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T10:14:18-07:00","id":1449268,"title":"","content":"I completely disagree. No one's under any obligation to create a welcoming space for bigots within their hobbies in the vague hope that somehow the bigots &quot;learn something someday.&quot; Experience has taught me that the primary thing they learn is that if they pretend to be nice, other white people will bend over backwards to keep the peace at the expanse of black, brown, and indigenous gamers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24383-laughinggull","name":"LaughingGull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24383_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T15:51:49-07:00","id":1449288,"title":"","content":"What was the question they had to answer?<br /> <br /> Not having a Confederate flag on your home page is a pretty low bar...<br /> <br /> Literally no one I talk to (about Scion or otherwise) does that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T20:11:01-07:00","id":1449305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tytalan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1442997-face-book-scion-group?p=1449210#post1449210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No IanWatson I don\u2019t think it was one of those. The Admin had a post up telling everyone they had to answer the question and if they had any pictures of the confederate flag on there home page they would not be allowed in. I posted that this was wrong that you shouldn\u2019t judge by such things be instead judge by their actions in the group. I was than called a racist and a Homophobe because I stuck up for freedom of beliefs. Someone else posted a stupid article claiming to tolerance is wrong and we should attack people that believe things we consider wrong. My comments were all along the lines that it\u2019s actions not beliefs that matter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Please think about what you are defending if you seriously want to defend white supremacy. To me as a non-American it is quite frankly shocking to see so many defend and glorify the abomination that the American South was. Yes, there is freedom of expression and opinions but not all opinions are worth equally much and do not need your sympathy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T18:13:50-07:00","id":1449406,"title":"","content":"Yeah, no. If you have a swastika on the wall, but promise to be nice, would that be okay? A banner of support for Islamic State? A KKK hood? A group has every right to say no to people if they display connections to belief systems that are against any decent code of conduct. And &quot;freedom of speech&quot; means you can belive or say whatever floats your boat, but I don't have to allow you in my club, on my page, or in my gaming group. Sometimes the best solution is for there to be harsh consequences for being part of something bad, not just being met with a blind eye in the name of tolerance and understanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5627,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","user":"Purple Snit","date":". 05-29-2021, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T00:44:35-07:00","id":1450145,"title":"","content":"Paradox of Tolerance, eh?<br /> Karl Popper had a lot to say about that, and frankly, not glorifying a slave-state would be a pretty low bar to pass.<br /> <br /> When the Tolerance begins to be subverted by the Intolerant, things are quickly going the wrong way. So, people take measures to protect themselves and their communities.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;unfriendly part of the Scion community&quot; - well, sometimes, feathers get ruffled. That much is certain. Often due to differences of how to approach topics of faith and culture in games. And while I don't like the vitriolic tone it can end up in some times, I cannot really say that people are completely wrong for taking a stance against repeating mistakes of the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":225,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","user":"Growls","date":". 05-29-2021, 03:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T18:37:59-07:00","id":1451091,"title":"","content":"You don\u2019t change Bigotry by attacking Bigots all you do than is encourage them to be even more intolerant. The supposed Paradox of Tolerance is a article that has been disproven over and again. It tells you that it\u2019s alright to persecute those that disagree with what you believe is right. You don\u2019t fight Bigotry with more Bigotry you fight it with Education. By excluding a group of people because of their beliefs you create a group that is disenfranchised and moved to more and more extreme actions. When you start punishing people for words and beliefs you force them to use guns and bombs. As long as a person is not breaking the rules of a group they should be allow to be a member as soon as you exclude them because of a picture on their personal FB page your being the Bigot. I\u2019m a Conservative no I\u2019m not a Bigot I embrace all people and tho I\u2019m a Christian I\u2019ve studied many religions and incorporated many of their philosophy into my own beliefs. Not once in that group did I attack anyone my only crime was Fighting a form of bigotry. I\u2019ve been told that I\u2019m automatically a Bigot because I was born in the 60s I find this funny because that statement itself is a form of bigotry. If your first response is to call someone a Homophobic or a Bigot because they disagree with you than the true Bigot is you. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6379-tytalan","name":"tytalan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T20:35:07-07:00","id":1451103,"title":"","content":"People still have the right to exclude someone from a club/social media page/gaming group they run if those people don't meet their expectations or requirements. It can be done in a more tactful way than stereotyping or insulting someone, yes, but it isn't up to them to say &quot;come on in, Mr. KKK, and let us enlighten you with our truths&quot;. I feel that you should move on and find a group more suited to your needs, and leave the one that refused you behind. It isn't worth your stress, and it isn't OP's problem either, since it isn't their group. Just my 2 cents' worth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T06:53:18-07:00","id":1451204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tytalan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1442997-face-book-scion-group?p=1451091#post1451091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don\u2019t change Bigotry by attacking Bigots all you do than is encourage them to be even more intolerant. The supposed Paradox of Tolerance is a article that has been disproven over and again. It tells you that it\u2019s alright to persecute those that disagree with what you believe is right. You don\u2019t fight Bigotry with more Bigotry you fight it with Education. By excluding a group of people because of their beliefs you create a group that is disenfranchised and moved to more and more extreme actions. When you start punishing people for words and beliefs you force them to use guns and bombs. As long as a person is not breaking the rules of a group they should be allow to be a member as soon as you exclude them because of a picture on their personal FB page your being the Bigot. I\u2019m a Conservative no I\u2019m not a Bigot I embrace all people and tho I\u2019m a Christian I\u2019ve studied many religions and incorporated many of their philosophy into my own beliefs. Not once in that group did I attack anyone my only crime was Fighting a form of bigotry. I\u2019ve been told that I\u2019m automatically a Bigot because I was born in the 60s I find this funny because that statement itself is a form of bigotry. If your first response is to call someone a Homophobic or a Bigot because they disagree with you than the true Bigot is you. </div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that you describe yourself as a \u201cconservative Christian\u201d tells me that you probably don\u2019t just feel badly for these people for being excluded; you probably actually sympathize with their beliefs, even if you don\u2019t go so far as to put a Confederate flag on your home page.<br /> <br /> Tolerance is important and a lot of conservative Christians are not very tolerant (though defo not all; my friend is a minister and even if he prays for your soul cause he thinks you\u2019re going to Hell for your beliefs he\u2019ll still hang out with you and be nice to you and help you put in your portable AC).<br /> <br /> As for your age, not everyone from that age group is a bigot, far from it, I learned tolerance from people who were born in the Sixties. In that respect I totally agree with you.<br /> <br /> I still say not having a Confederate flag on your home page is a pretty low bar. If you openly display the battle flag of a country that persecuted and enslaved and even raped people of color as the first thing I see about you...that\u2019s not someone I\u2019d wanna hang out and talk about Scion with either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 06-07-2021, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021